message: "If you use this software, please cite the associated paper."
title: "From Jumps to Signatures: A Generative Method for Temporal Point Processes"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Cariou-Kotlarek"
    given-names: "Niels"
    affiliation: "University College London"
  - family-names: "Lampos"
    given-names: "Vasileios"
    affiliation: "University College London"
abstract: >-
  Rough path signatures provide a universal feature map for continuous paths and,
  via the expected signature, a principled characterisation of path distributions.
  These results do not directly extend to the cadlag paths of temporal point
  processes (TPPs), limiting the use of signature methods for event sequences.
  This work introduces the interarrival embedding, a stable (homeomorphic) lift
  from jump paths to continuous paths of bounded variation, enabling signature
  methods on discrete event sequences. Building on it, SigTPP is the first
  signature-based generative model for TPPs, trained with a path-level loss on
  complete trajectories. The same construction yields three distributional
  discrepancies on counting-path space for evaluating generative TPP models.
  Across synthetic and real-world datasets, SigTPP achieves the best average rank
  across eight complementary metrics and improves against every baseline by at
  least 19 percent on average.
keywords:
  - temporal point processes
  - generative models
  - path signatures
  - rough paths
  - Wasserstein distance
